0028:   // ==== list(seq) — materialize a list/tuple into a list (e.g. list(d.keys())) ==
0029:   // Minimal: the "copy a sequence" case (list of a list is itself; list of a tuple keeps order).
0030:   // list() of other iterables (str/range/set/zip) is added via the iterator fold when needed.
0031:   // (k-cell — list() constructs a NEW object)
0032:   rule <k> #applyK(toCall(builtinV("list")), (list(VS:ValSeq),  .Vals)) => #alloc(list(VS)) ... </k>
